        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: معائنہ کرنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "معائنہ کرنا — muāinā karnā — \"to examine (a patient)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ڈاکٹر نے مریض کا معائنہ کیا۔ ḍākṭar ne marīz kā muāinā kiyā. The doctor examined the patient."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے بچے کا معائنہ کیا, us ne bachche kā muāinā kiyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "معائنہ کرنا (muāinā karnā) is built from معائنہ, usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic muʿāyana, \"looking at closely\", and کرنا, \"to do\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
